"""Write the final repair report using measured artifacts; no success is inferred."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib,sys,tarfile
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];OUT=ROOT/'runs/locomotion/csdog_curriculum_v6_1/repair_20261027';RUNS=OUT.parent
sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'src'))

def main():
    old=json.loads((OUT/'old_status.json').read_text());selection=json.loads((OUT/'history_selection.json').read_text());ab=json.loads((OUT/'ab_selection.json').read_text())
    originals=json.loads((OUT/'v6_checkpoint_sha256.json').read_text());changed=[f for f,h in originals.items() if not (ROOT/f).exists() or hashlib.sha256((ROOT/f).read_bytes()).hexdigest()!=h]
    if changed:raise RuntimeError('Protected V6 checkpoint changed: '+str(changed))
    verified=dict(v6_checkpoints=len(originals),changed=changed)
    (OUT/'final_protection_verification.json').write_text(json.dumps(verified,indent=2))
    runtime=json.loads((OUT/'launch_verification.json').read_text()) if (OUT/'launch_verification.json').exists() else dict(status='NOT_STARTED',reason=ab['status'])
    if not runtime.get('training_started',False):
        import time
        from dogfight.locomotion.curriculum_v6_1.supervisor import atomic_json,SCORE_VERSION
        atomic_json(OUT/'TRAINING_STATUS.json',dict(training_status='BLOCKED_NEEDS_REDESIGN',diagnosis=ab['status'],stage_name='FORWARD',substage='1B',total_updates=1000,arm_updates={'A':500,'B':500},best_checkpoint=selection['checkpoint'],heartbeat_unix=time.time(),long_training_started=False,score_version=SCORE_VERSION))
        (OUT/'STATUS_SUMMARY.md').write_text('# V6.1 BLOCKED\n\nA: 500/500 updates; B: 500/500 updates. Both lost four-leg periodic gait relative to initialization. No long training process or service was launched. Preserved checkpoint: '+selection['checkpoint']+'\n')
        atomic_json(OUT/'CONTINUATION_GATE.json',dict(allowed=False,reason=ab['status']))
    lines=['# V6.1 repair report',f"V6 final stop: {old['total_updates']} executed PPO updates; Stage 1/FORWARD; `USER_SIGNAL_15`, process had already exited before this repair began. Recorded old PID 348960 was absent. Original parsed launch arguments are preserved in old_launch.json; because the process had already exited, its exact /proc argv and cwd could no longer be read. `interrupted.pt` was verified at update8460 with actor/critic, optimizer, std, LR, RNG, supervisor, course and repair history. `latest.pt` was only update8000 and was not used as the latest snapshot. Active candidate: none.",f"Original checkpoint protection: {len(originals)} files SHA256 checked, changes {len(changed)}. Full source backup: `source_before.tar.gz`. No original model/URDF/STL/PD/torque/joint-map/observations/network/official Isaac Lab source was changed. Per-run asset verification files are retained.",'## Supervisor repairs','Continuous slip cost is -0.35*log1p(slip/0.08), with dominant signed movement progress and separate stop/yaw costs. Slip 0.30 to 0.15 improves the motion score continuously; the strict slip acceptance limit remains 0.08 m/s. Ranking first preserves previous-stage qualifications and verified continuation safety, then applies continuous score. Every valid full checkpoint, including both candidate arms and rollback reviews, is registered. Protocol/score/contact versions and seeds separate incomparable evidence. Historical JSON scores remain untouched; derived re-scoring and new common physical evaluations are saved independently.','Failed completed-swing 0.15->0.30 is explicitly remembered. Further repairs choose one factor from actual gait/slip/stop/PPO/direction evidence, retain before/after parameters and matched control/adjusted outcomes, and block on repeat failures or repair exhaustion. Repair cooldown does not claim an improvement. Regression guards compare matching speed/seed rows so an already-failed speed case cannot hide loss of the previously working gait.','## Contact findings and correction','Raw contact force flags agree with geometry in sampled traces. Short near-ground unloads and physical chatter coexist with genuine air motion. Crucially, 50Hz sampling can alias intervening contacts or clearance failures into apparent >=60ms swings. The first proxy-based A branch was safely stopped before any additional PPO update (checkpoint counter6000) when this was found. It is retained as an aborted preflight, not counted in the final A/B.','The revised implementation uses integer 2ms physical ticks over all environments. Each failed raw condition breaks continuous air time; there is no hysteresis, deleted event, or gap merging. Original 50Hz fields are retained. Real 15mm/60ms thresholds are unchanged, and support slip is measured over actual physical substep supports. All four historical checkpoints were physically re-evaluated with this protocol. Detailed records and all four historical physical videos are linked in `CONTACT_AND_GAIT_DIAGNOSIS.md`.','## Gait and stop changes','The original progress4.0/tracking2.0 rewards, policy architecture, observations, hardware and Stage2/3/4 course remain shared. Internal Stage1A preserves forward motion; Stage1B adds translation-conditioned continuous swing guidance and physically verified completed landings. Completed landings additionally require >2cm of commanded foot placement, so pure vertical lifting earns no completed-swing reward. Guidance requires actual clearance, no shin contact, forward foot excursion and relative speed, continued body progress and remaining supports. The measured 20–40ms fragments receive no guidance. Stage1C adds only gradual quality costs and 25% stop sampling after a full 500Hz panel confirms four-leg periodic gait. Original Stage1 acceptance still requires three consecutive full passes of all original criteria.','Zero commands are checked at Actor observation indices9:12 and stored exactly in physical trajectories. Stop reward is already zero-command gated and uses full translation norm and yaw squared; guidance gives no stationary reward. Stop evaluation uses speed norm and mean absolute yaw, including oscillation that a signed mean hides. Any increased stop sampling is declared in the effective configuration and tested as part of the chosen branch.','## Historical ranking',f"Selected physical starting policy: `{selection['checkpoint']}`; continuous score {selection['score']:.6f}. Detailed ranking: `HISTORICAL_CHECKPOINT_RANKING.md`; physical metrics: `HISTORICAL_CHECKPOINT_METRICS.md`. The selected policy has useful forward motion but is not declared a Stage1 graduate.",'## Validation and A/B',f"CPU regression log: `unit_tests_verified.log`. Real 2-update smoke and exact policy/optimizer/LR round trip: `{RUNS}/repair_smoke_verified_20261027/checkpoint_restore_test.json`. Full A/B results, training curves, capability plots and CSV: `V6_1_AB_COMPARISON.md`.", '```json',json.dumps(ab,indent=2),'```','## Restoration and actual runtime','The actor, critic, optimizer momentum, learned exploration std, LR and RNG are fully restored without architectural migration. RNG is restored before reset to make candidate initial perturbations comparable. Supervisor ranking is versioned and reset on migration; source history and stage counters are retained. Physics solver caches/episode state are reset, so this is not bit-exact simulation continuation. Global counters follow the selected branch lineage; old V6 still retains its8460-update cumulative history.','```json',json.dumps(runtime,indent=2),'```','The implemented manager can launch a detached local watcher independently of Codex. If runtime above is BLOCKED, no watcher or long trainer was launched, and post-session survival/100-update live-service checks were intentionally not run because the safety gate failed. The trainer handles STOP/SIGTERM at PPO boundaries, writes complete checkpoints atomically, evaluates at250/500 updates, gates courses, performs bounded local repairs and stops on unresolved severe faults or low disk space. No fixed total iteration cap is imposed.','## Evidence links','[Contact diagnosis](CONTACT_AND_GAIT_DIAGNOSIS.md) · [Historical ranking](HISTORICAL_CHECKPOINT_RANKING.md) · [A/B comparison](V6_1_AB_COMPARISON.md)']
    (OUT/'V6_1_REPAIR_REPORT.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
    with tarfile.open(OUT/'v6_1_source_release.tar.gz','w:gz') as tar:
        for p in [ROOT/'src/dogfight/locomotion/curriculum_v6_1',ROOT/'configs/locomotion/curriculum_v6_1',ROOT/'scripts/train/csdog_curriculum_v6_1.py',ROOT/'scripts/evaluate/csdog_curriculum_v6_1.py',ROOT/'scripts/diagnostics/curriculum_v6_1_supervisor.py',ROOT/'tests/test_curriculum_v6_1.py']:
            tar.add(p,arcname=str(p.relative_to(ROOT)),filter=lambda x:None if '__pycache__' in x.name else x)
    print(json.dumps(dict(report=str(OUT/'V6_1_REPAIR_REPORT.md'),protection=verified,runtime=runtime.get('status'))))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
